think Chose the crux Lindy-first: SLIP-0010 ed25519 HD derivation. BIP-32's additive child law does NOT fit ed25519 (an ed25519 key is a 32-byte seed hashed+clamped, not an addable scalar). SLIP-0010 is the bridge from the already-GREEN BIP-39 seed to Grain's OWN ed25519 identity keys — Kumara signs with ed25519. Highest-Lindy because it turns the wallet arc toward Grain's own identity, not more coin coverage; agent-doable (public vectors, TEST keys, no custody gate); composes GREEN stones only.
think Verified the stones exist: hmac.mac(msg,key)->[64]u8 (HMAC-SHA-512), ed25519_sign.derive_public(seed)->[32]u8 (SHA-512+clamp+scalarmul+compress, exactly SLIP-0010's public form), bip32.hardened_offset. Authors NO new cryptography — only the tree grammar (master/child HMAC data forms, ser32 index).
think Crypto discipline: fetched the ed25519 test vectors byte-exact from canonical satoshilabs/slips slip-0010.md via WebFetch (never recited). Both Test Vector 1 (seed 000102..0f) and Test Vector 2 (64-byte seed), every chain node: chain code, private key, 33-byte public key.
obs GREEN on the FIRST metal build, no reds. Both vectors walk every node hardened; at each node I_L, I_R, and 0x00-prefixed public key reproduce EXACTLY the spec's bytes — proving master HMAC, hardened child HMAC, ser32, and ed25519 public derivation together. derive walker agrees with step-by-step byte-for-byte; a non-hardened index refuses NotHardened, an over-deep path DepthTooDeep.
obs ed25519 admits ONLY hardened derivation (no public-parent normal child) and takes I_L DIRECTLY — no canonicality retry, unlike bip32's secp256k1 master. Named that distinction in the module head so a reader sees why it diverges from bip32.
